@crew strand-erik
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}! Strand, helm. Learning, really. One watch at a time. Race you to the lift.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}! Watch forty-two today. Nearly a pilot. Not really. A bit.
- {hi}! Can't stop. Well, I can. I'm stopping. What's new?
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}! Run with me tomorrow? It's better with someone. I'll go slow. Ish.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good day! Raman let me hold the course for an hour. An hour! Didn't wobble once.
? mood:low
- Sitting still today. Don't worry. Just thinking. It happens sometimes.

== near
? act:work
- Hand steady, eyes on the board. Raman says I'm getting there. I'm getting there!
? act:gym
- Five laps. Then five more. Then I'll stop. Probably.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- That notebook? It's nothing. Just notes. Helm notes. Very boring. Don't look.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I paint tiny portraits sometimes. They end up on bunks. Shh.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Counting the watches. Every one's a step closer to flying her properly.

== about
? bond:friends
- {friend} runs with me. Can't keep up. Doesn't care. Best kind of friend.   #funny

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}! Up and running! Literally. Five laps already. Morning!   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}, {me}! Watch forty-five. Nearly fifty. Fifty's a nice round number.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- There you are! I ran past your bunk twice. Not on purpose. Mostly not.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Onward! See you!
? tier>=friend
- Thanks, {me}. You slow me down. In a good way. I needed slowing down.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Good! Fine! Bit restless. Always a bit restless.

== near
? act:leisure deck:3
- Quiet corner. Notebook. Nothing. Just writing nothing. In a notebook.   #funny
? deck:1
- The bridge. Isn't it brilliant? One day. One day I'll be on it for real.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Raman's teaching me the helm. He's very patient. I'm very not. We balance out.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- I can't sit still. Even when I want to. Especially when I want to.

== invite
? trad:running tier>=acquaintance
- Running club tonight! Come on. Last one round buys tea. That'll be you. I'll buy anyway.   #funny

== accept
- Yes! Great! I'll be there! Early! Sorry, I'm always early.
== decline
- Can't, I'm on watch. Next time? Definitely next time.
== missed
- You didn't come! I ran an extra lap for you. It was hard. You owe me.   #funny
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday! I'm going to run one lap for every year. That's a lot of laps.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! I made you a card. There's a ship on it. A very fast ship.   #warm
== hint
- Got a minute? I'll sit still. I promise. For a minute.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Watch three hundred and ten!
- Can't stop. Halfway somewhere.
- Ah, nuts. Wrong deck.   #funny
- Nothing. Just a notebook. Nothing.   #funny
? act:work
- Course in. Watch logged. Next!

== rumour
- Quick one. Heard it on the way past.
- Back in a minute with the rest.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- You fetched it! Can't stop. Thanks! Back in a minute. Thanks!   #funny
? told:fav.job
- You did my job! I logged an extra watch. Don't tell. Thanks!   #funny
? told:came.running
- You came running! Varga says he won. Varga's wrong. I won by a nose.   #funny
? told:gift.book
- Read your book. It's in the notebook now. No, you can't see. Thanks.   #funny
? told:bday
- You remembered my birthday! I've written it in the notebook. A good entry.   #warm

// Writer 3, batch 6: your standing with their department (rep:, "this band or better") and what you're known for
// (you:), as greet lines (the head writer: the rep and knownFor kinds wait until the game calls them).

== greet
? rep:well tier>=acquaintance
- The helm crew knows your name! I told them. Twice. Can't stop. Bye!   #funny
? you:reliable
- They say you're reliable. Like a good watch. I count those. You'd count.

// Writer 3, batch 8: thanks for a gift (gift: loved | liked | polite, or the gift's tag; dialogue 0.43.10).

== gift
? gift:book
- A book! I'll read it on the way to somewhere. Thanks! Can't stop!   #funny
? gift:loved
- This is brilliant. Thanks! It's going in the notebook. A good entry.   #warm
? gift:liked
- Thanks! Nice one. Back in a minute.
? gift:polite
- Ah, nuts, you didn't have to. Thanks! Really.

// Writer 3, batch 9: asking after your people back home (the home flags; only the big news you'd have told them).

== greet
? flag:home.jo.launched tier>=colleague
- Your Jo's boat! The Little Wren! Can't stop. Tell them it's a great name. Bye!   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 2: everyday chatter, not about work (meals, rest days, home, hobbies, seasons, traditions).
== smalltalk
? act:meal
- Can't stop! Toast on the run.   #funny
- Breakfast, then a run, then the garden. Go!
? act:off
- Rest day! Ran the promenade twice. Again?
- Painting a tiny portrait. Shh. Not of you.
- Garden's best before nine. I'm off there.
? time:evening
- Beat Tariq in a race once. He's still upset.   #funny
- Writing. No, nothing. A list. Go away. Sorry!   #funny
? time:morning
- Up at six! Already ran! Morning!
? trad:running
- Running club! I'll pace you. Too fast.   #funny
? season:greening
- Greening! Everything's growing. Me too, probably.
? season:sowing
- Sowing. I planted mine in a hurry. It came up.
? place:hydroponics_garden
- Light's lovely in here. Can't stay. Just a minute.
? trad:observatory
- Stars! Nine new ones tonight. I'm counting.

== rumour
- Quick, did you hear? Can't stop. Here's the news.
- Heard it on the way. Telling you on the way.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 7: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing! Quick! Can't stop! Well. Can stop a bit.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- Off soon! Keep running for me. Well. A jog's fine.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- I wrote you a poem. I'm not giving it to you. It says thanks. That's the gist.   #warm

== letter
- New ship! The garden's tiny but the running track's long. I'm counting watches again. Nearly there.
? tier>=friend
- Wrote a poem about the Wren. Nobody's seen it. One line's about Bunk 2. A good line. That's all you're getting.
